The program of run-arrays.m, run on the machine's GPU: the arrays the
region updates are mapped tofrom, over their headers' and elements' words.
A region whose procedure updates an array, which its operations do not
show, maps each array of the type tofrom and finds which one it gives
(design document, "What is lowered so far"), so the array it only reads
is copied back too, unchanged.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/run-arrays.m -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIBOMPTARGET_INFO=1 %t 2> %t.info \
RUN:   | FileCheck %S/run-arrays.m --check-prefix=OUTPUT --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.info
CHECK: info: Entering OpenMP kernel at {{.*}}run-arrays.m:{{[0-9]+}}:5 with 6 arguments:
CHECK-NEXT: info: to(region_slot)[8]
CHECK-NEXT: info: tofrom(A)[32]
CHECK-NEXT: info: tofrom(STATE_VARIABLE_B_0)[40]
CHECK: info: Entering OpenMP kernel at {{.*}}run-arrays.m:{{[0-9]+}}:5 with 7 arguments:
CHECK-NEXT: info: to(region_slot)[8]
CHECK-NEXT: info: tofrom(STATE_VARIABLE_B_0)[16]
CHECK-NEXT: info: tofrom(STATE_VARIABLE_C_0)[24]
CHECK-NOT: Entering OpenMP kernel
